.TH SUPER-KILIX 6 "2026" "super-kilix 0.0.1" "Games"
.SH NAME
super-kilix \- an original side-scrolling platformer starring Kilix
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B super-kilix
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B super-kilix
is a side-scrolling platformer for Kitty-graphics terminals. Kilix, an orange
star-vault salvager, runs, jumps, and boosts a micro-thruster across a long
horizontal journey through the derelict star-vaults of his own machine world.
All art is drawn at runtime from soft-raster primitives and all sound is
synthesised in memory; the game ships no asset files.
.PP
Run without arguments in a Kitty-protocol terminal to play. The options below
drive deterministic, headless operation for testing and inspection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-selftest " [seed] [ticks]"
Run a deterministic simulation for the given seed and tick count (default
1337 and 12000) and print a PASS line.
.TP
.B \-\-rules\-test
Run the simulation-rule fixtures.
.TP
.B \-\-input\-test
Run the input-funnel fixtures.
.TP
.BI \-\-render\-test " [seed]"
Render the scene corpus and check renderer purity.
.TP
.B \-\-sound\-test
Exercise every sound. Returns success even with no audio sink.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump\-level " N"
Print a vault's layout for inspection.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUPER_KILIX_DATA_HOME
Override the profile parent directory.
.TP
.B SUPER_KILIX_NO_PROFILE
Disable profile persistence (set automatically in headless modes).
.TP
.B SUPER_KILIX_RENDER_DIR
Directory for render-test output.
.TP
.B SUPER_KILIX_SKIP_PROBE
Skip the terminal capability probe.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kitty (1)
